211	   * nobody" in any case: a test with no personas produces no simulations, so it
212	   * could never run. Leaving the set alone is what leaving the field out does.
213	   */
214	  readonly personaIds?: readonly string[];
215	  /**
216	   * The tools the next version should answer for itself.
217	   *
218	   * An empty list means here what it means on a create — override nothing —
219	   * because overriding nothing is a state a test can be in and is the one most
220	   * tests are in. So `[]` clears the overrides, and leaving the field out keeps
221	   * them.
222	   */
223	  readonly mockOverrides?: readonly MockOverrideInput[];
224	  /**
225	   * The version this edit was written against, when the writer knows it.
226	   *
227	   * A precondition rather than a change, and it rides here because it belongs
228	   * to the same write: it is compared under the lock the edit already takes, so
229	   * there is no moment between checking and writing for a second writer to
230	   * arrive in. A mismatch refuses everything with `TestMovedOnError`.

